# The shell scripts and the supervisord configuration are copied into a Linux
# container image. A CRLF line ending survives the copy, and the kernel then
# looks for an interpreter whose name ends in a carriage return, which fails
# with an error message that names the right file and the wrong reason.
#
# The development machine checks out with autocrlf enabled, so without these
# rules the next checkout would quietly produce an image that cannot start.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
